<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23576" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-nūbo</span></b> , psi, ptum, 3,
			v. n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>to marry into.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quae haud facile iis, in quibus nata erat,
					humiliora sineret ea, quae innupsisset,</span>”
				<i>into which she had married</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					1, 34, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nostris thalamis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					7, 856</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>to pass over</i>,
			Lucil. ap. <i><span class="en">Non. 125, 10</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
